
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@userAToken = user-a-token
@userBToken = user-b-token
@adminToken = admin-token

### 1. Project greeting (no authentication required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/greeting


### 2. Get all assignments as User A
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 3. Get all assignments as User B
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{userBToken}}


### 4. Get all assignments as Admin
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 5. Filter assignments by course
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments?course=Machine%20Learning
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 6. Filter assignments by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 7. Filter assignments by deadline
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments?deadline_before=2026-11-25
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 8. Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments?page=1&per_page=2
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 9. Get a specific assignment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments/assignment_101
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 10. Create an assignment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Complete API Documentation",
    "description": "Prepare the documentation for the StudyFlow AI API.",
    "course": "Software Engineering",
    "deadline": "2026-11-30",
    "priority": "high",
    "status": "pending"
}


### 11. Update an assignment
# Replace assignment_105 with the ID returned by the create request.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments/assignment_105
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "Updated API Documentation",
    "description": "Complete and review the StudyFlow AI API documentation.",
    "course": "Software Engineering",
    "deadline": "2026-12-01",
    "priority": "medium",
    "status": "in_progress"
}


### 12. Delete an assignment
# Replace assignment_105 with the ID you want to delete.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments/assignment_105
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 13. Test missing authentication
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments


### 14. Test invalid authentication
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token


### 15. Test accessing another user's assignment
# User A should not be able to access User B's assignment.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments/assignment_103
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 16. Test a nonexistent assignment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments/assignment_999
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### 17. Test invalid assignment data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "A",
    "description": "",
    "course": "M",
    "deadline": "invalid-date",
    "priority": "urgent",
    "status": "unknown"
}
